		{
			description: [
				"Source moves by relay, within a radius, and it does not care what is between them."
				""
				"This is the opposite of a mana spreader in every respect, which is exactly why people who learn Leaf first keep building the Song wrong. No line of sight. No bursts. Just range."
			]
			id: "3118DFF53DB85E19"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Song"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4EC993E45E0AC934"
				title: "Jars Hold, Relays Carry"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Jars Hold, Relays Carry"
			x: 1.5d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"A spell is read left to right and it is strict."
				""
				"The Form comes first and decides the shape - touch, projectile, self. Then the Effects, in order. Then Augments, which modify the effect immediately before them, not the whole spell."
				""
				"An Amplify in the wrong slot amplifies the wrong thing. The Scribe's Table will let you do it, too."
			]
			id: "679BABEB09D97FEC"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Song"
			tasks: [{
				id: "22C0C682B782F36C"
				title: "Form, Then Effect, Then Augment"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Form, Then Effect, Then Augment"
			x: 3.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The book has a mana bar of its own and each glyph you add makes the spell dearer."
				""
				"A three-glyph spell you can cast eight times is worth more than a six-glyph spell you can cast twice. Restraint is a mechanic here, not a virtue."
			]
			id: "434945AA4A45BDA8"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Song"
			tasks: [{
				id: "69E914F20F62321B"
				title: "Every Glyph Costs"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Every Glyph Costs"
			x: 4.5d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Glyphs are not found. They are written, from experience and reagents, at the table."
				""
				"Unlock them deliberately. The book will only hold what you have scribed, and the reagent for a glyph is usually a hint about what it does."
			]
			id: "18CA7FFBED0425CB"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Song"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4674181C7BC6FCBA"
				title: "The Scribe's Table"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Scribe's Table"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"You have an altar now, so here is the bill."
				""
				"Every infusion takes aura from the chunk it happens in. The chunk does not refill on a timer and there is no reservoir underneath. Work in one place long enough and the land there will stop working at all - and it will show, visibly, in the world."
				""
				"Move your altar. Or plant. Those are the two answers and there is not a third."
			]
			id: "497CF83575982643"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Nature's Aura"
			tasks: [{
				id: "751573121A73D451"
				title: "What You Draw Down Stays Down"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "What You Draw Down Stays Down"
			x: 7.5d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Before the ground fails it warns you."
				""
				"Colour goes out of the grass. The aura blooms stop appearing. Read the warning and move; ignore it and you will be standing in a second Ashen Grove of your own making."
				""
				"That is not a metaphor I am reaching for. It is the mechanic, and it is what happened here."
			]
			id: "3FAB1DBB2124415F"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Nature's Aura"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5B335EAD25424A5D"
				title: "The Land Tells You First"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Land Tells You First"
			x: 9.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Chalk on stone, candles at the points, and the shape must close."
				""
				"A pentacle with a gap is not a weaker pentacle, it is nothing at all. Count your glyphs before you light anything."
				""
				"What you call is bound by the circle, and the circle is only as good as its worst line."
			]
			id: "1962108635B9D8A0"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Occultism"
